          "source_page_numbers": [
            3
          ]
        }
      ],
      "mark_scheme_items": [
        {
          "sequence_number": 1,
          "mark_code": "B1",
          "content_markdown": "$$4k + k + 4k + 9k = 1, k = \\frac{1}{18}$$",
          "guidance_markdown": "Using sum of probabilities = 1 to form an equation in $$k$$ or value of $$k$$ stated.",
          "is_final_answer": false,
          "is_alternative_method": false,
          "source_page_numbers": [
            9
          ]
        },
        {
          "sequence_number": 2,
          "mark_code": "B1",
          "content_markdown": "$$x$$ -2 1 2 3\n$$P(X = x)$$ $$\\frac{4}{18}$$ $$\\frac{1}{18}$$ $$\\frac{4}{18}$$ $$\\frac{9}{18}$$ | $$X$$ -2 1 2 3\n$$P(X = x)$$ $$4k$$ $$k$$ $$4k$$ $$9k$$\nCondone extra $$X$$ values if probability stated as 0.",
          "guidance_markdown": "Table with at least 2 correctly linked probabilities accurate. May be in terms of $$k$$.",
          "is_final_answer": false,
          "is_alternative_method": false,
          "source_page_numbers": [
            9
          ]
        },
        {
          "sequence_number": 3,
          "mark_code": "B1",
          "content_markdown": "",
          "guidance_markdown": "4 correctly linked probabilities accurate. May not be in a table.",
          "is_final_answer": true,
          "is_alternative_method": false,
          "source_page_numbers": [
            9
          ]
        },
        {
          "sequence_number": 4,
          "mark_code": "B1 FT",
          "content_markdown": "$$[E(X) = 28k =] \\frac{14}{9}, 1.56$$",
          "guidance_markdown": "**FT** $$28 \\times \\text{their } k$$ **or** correct with $$0 < p < 1$$.",
          "is_final_answer": true,
          "is_alternative_method": false,
          "source_page_numbers": [
            9
          ]
        },
        {
          "sequence_number": 5,
          "mark_code": "M1",
          "content_markdown": "$$P(X \\neq 2 | X > 0) = \\frac{10}{18} \\bigg/ \\frac{14}{18}$$",
          "guidance_markdown": "$$\\frac{\\text{their } P(1) + P(3)}{\\text{their } P(1) + P(2) + P(3)}$$. May be in terms of $$k$$. With $$0 < p < 1$$. If table correct, accept $$\\frac{10}{18} \\bigg/ \\frac{14}{18}$$ **or** $$\\frac{5}{9} \\bigg/ \\frac{7}{9}$$.",
